<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh's Mongla port workers call off strike.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh's Mongla port workers call off strike.</headline>
<dateline>KHULNA, Bangladesh 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers, demanding higher wages, called off two days of strike and resumed work on Monday night, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling came to a halt on Saturday night as stevedores refused to engage workers after about 300 men working in one section walked out demanding higher wages, the officials said.</p>
<p>The officials said the strike, which stranded 18 ships, ended after the workers returned on the promise that the authorities would try to solve the wage dispute between the port labourers' and stevedores' association.</p>
</text>
